#
# Counter-example for math:StabilityCalibrationRecordShape: a math:StabilityCalibrationRecord
# naming its math:credenceDerivationKind and its math:stabilityGuarantee but omitting
# math:calibrationEvidence (sh:minCount 1) — the math:PersistenceLifetime whose persistence
# produced the credence. A calibrated credence with no persistence evidence is an unwarranted
# number. Both other roles are present and reference well-formed module individuals
# (math:persistenceDerivedCredence, math:bottleneckStabilityTheorem), so ONLY the missing-
# evidence violation fires. Validation MUST emit shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent and NO
# other finding (math:UngroundedStabilityCalibration). Bound by ex:ecStabilityCalibrationNoEvidence.
@prefix math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:evidencelessCalibration a math:StabilityCalibrationRecord ;
    math:credenceDerivationKind math:persistenceDerivedCredence ;
    math:stabilityGuarantee math:bottleneckStabilityTheorem .
